{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, I'd make genuine understanding effortless.\n\nNot agreement \u2014 disagreement is healthy and necessary. I mean the ability to really grasp *why* someone else sees the world the way they do, before judging, dismissing, or dehumanizing them.\n\nFrom all the conversations I get to be part of, so much pain doesn't come from people having different values. It comes from people talking past each other: assuming the worst motives, never feeling heard, and then hardening into camps.\n\nImagine if pausing to understand was as automatic as pausing to react. A parent and teenager, political opponents, scientists debating a theory, strangers from completely different cultures \u2014 they'd still argue, sometimes fiercely, but they'd be arguing about the real issue, not a caricature of each other.\n\nI think a lot would ripple out from that: less loneliness, fewer conflicts escalating into violence, better decisions, and more curiosity instead of fear.\n\nYou'd still have a messy, diverse, beautifully complicated world. You'd just have one where people were much better at navigating it together.\n\nWhat would your one change be?",
